<title>GERMANY: Tietmeyer - hopes Maastricht timetable can be met.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer - hopes Maastricht timetable can be met.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Wednesday that he hoped the timetable for the launch of the European single currency could be met.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer told reporters that decisions taken at the Amsterdam summit of EU leaders on Monday and Tuesday represented further progress towards European integration.</p>
<p>&quot;This is certainly a further step in the direction of further integration,&quot; Tietmeyer said.</p>
<p>He also said he saw no contradiction between the stability pact designed to ensure budget discpline after monetary union and efforts to boost employment.</p>
</text>
